      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.02,
          "end": 4.07,
          "en": "So we are fetching the expenses,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.07,
          "end": 5.47,
          "en": "we are getting them here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.47,
          "end": 9.028,
          "en": "but how can we now use them in a recentExpenses?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.028,
          "end": 11.14,
          "en": "Well, we could for example say",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.14,
          "end": 14.59,
          "en": "that we are no longer interested in the context here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.59,
          "end": 16.23,
          "en": "hence I will comment this out.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.23,
          "end": 19.12,
          "en": "I will not delete it because we will use it again later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.12,
          "end": 21.66,
          "en": "But for the moment I will comment it out.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 21.66,
          "end": 24.42,
          "en": "And that instead, whenever we visit recentExpenses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 25.3,
          "end": 29.56,
          "en": "we want to actually trigger this code here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.56,
          "end": 31.593,
          "en": "and fetch our expenses.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.63,
          "end": 34.84,
          "en": "And therefore, since we get our expenses here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 34.84,
          "end": 38.573,
          "en": "we could manage some state here in recentExpenses,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 39.75,
          "end": 42.248,
          "en": "and we would have our fetchedExpenses here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 42.248,
          "end": 44.165,
          "en": "and setfetchedExpenses,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 45.44,
          "end": 47.93,
          "en": "and initially this could be an MT array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 47.93,
          "end": 49.98,
          "en": "And then here, once we got our expenses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 49.98,
          "end": 52.854,
          "en": "we call setfetchedExpenses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 52.854,
          "end": 56.283,
          "en": "and set this equal 2D expenses we got here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 57.64,
          "end": 59.382,
          "en": "And then this state will be updated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 59.382,
          "end": 61.9,
          "en": "after we fetched our expenses.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 61.9,
          "end": 64.95,
          "en": "So therefore we can then use these fetchedExpenses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 64.95,
          "end": 66.52,
          "en": "in this component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 66.52,
          "end": 69.15,
          "en": "So instead of expensesCtx.expenses,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 69.15,
          "end": 73.84,
          "en": "we work with our fetchedExpenses here and we filter those,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 73.84,
          "end": 76.94,
          "en": "and we therefor generate our recentExpenses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 76.94,
          "end": 79.28999999999999,
          "en": "based on the fetchedExpenses.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 79.28999999999999,
          "end": 83.17,
          "en": "Now, if we do all of that and we save this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 83.17,
          "end": 87.19,
          "en": "and we make sure that we here have an expense that is recent",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 87.19,
          "end": 89.57,
          "en": "and therefore I will edit it here on Firebase,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 89.57,
          "end": 92.72999999999999,
          "en": "which we can do to ensure that it is recent,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 92.72999999999999,
          "end": 96.223,
          "en": "that it is within the last seven days for me here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 97.15,
          "end": 101.24000000000001,
          "en": "If we do all of that and we force a reload",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 101.24000000000001,
          "end": 103.287,
          "en": "we will notice that initially there is this message",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 103.287,
          "end": 107.43,
          "en": "that we have no expenses for a very short duration,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 107.43,
          "end": 110.78,
          "en": "that is the duration where the request is on its way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 110.78,
          "end": 112.78999999999999,
          "en": "and we are waiting for the response,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 112.78999999999999,
          "end": 115.96000000000001,
          "en": "and thereafter we can see the fetched data here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 115.96000000000001,
          "end": 118.58,
          "en": "So fetching does work,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 118.58,
          "end": 121.12,
          "en": "however, one problem we will have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 121.12,
          "end": 123.9,
          "en": "is that if I add a new expense.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 123.9,
          "end": 127.643,
          "en": "So let's say this expense which is all the recent here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 128.87,
          "end": 130.65,
          "en": "it's not showing up here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 130.65,
          "end": 133.08,
          "en": "Now it is stored on the backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 133.08,
          "end": 135.81,
          "en": "We can see this newly added expense here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 136.66,
          "end": 138.75,
          "en": "but it's not available on the front end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 138.75,
          "end": 142.9,
          "en": "I need to reload my app to refetch it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 142.9,
          "end": 147.12,
          "en": "And then it is here, but that is of course not optimal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 147.12,
          "end": 148.563,
          "en": "Now, why is this happening?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 149.43,
          "end": 153.09,
          "en": "This is happening because the recentExpenses component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 153.09,
          "end": 156.07999999999998,
          "en": "actually wasn't removed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 156.07999999999998,
          "end": 158.07,
          "en": "When I manage a new expense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 158.07,
          "end": 161.54,
          "en": "this recent expense component is still in the background,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 161.54,
          "end": 163.05,
          "en": "it's not destroyed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 163.05,
          "end": 165.25,
          "en": "because we use the Stack Navigator,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 165.25,
          "end": 169.1,
          "en": "and there, if we push a new screen onto that stack",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 169.1,
          "end": 172.88,
          "en": "as we're doing it here with the manage expense screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 172.88,
          "end": 174.23,
          "en": "the old screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 174.23,
          "end": 177.05,
          "en": "So the recentExpenses screen here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 177.05,
          "end": 178.82,
          "en": "still runs in the background",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 178.82,
          "end": 181.37,
          "en": "no matter if we are on iOS or Android.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 181.37,
          "end": 183.6,
          "en": "On Android we don't see the old screen anymore",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 183.6,
          "end": 186.61,
          "en": "but it's also still running in the background.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 186.61,
          "end": 190.29,
          "en": "That means that when we close the managed expense screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 190.29,
          "end": 192.283,
          "en": "we don't recreate recentExpenses,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 193.19,
          "end": 195.16,
          "en": "instead it was always there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 195.16,
          "end": 198,
          "en": "Hence use a fact doesn't execute again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 198,
          "end": 199.75,
          "en": "and therefore we don't fetch again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 200.77,
          "end": 203.66,
          "en": "Now you might be able to find a workaround",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 203.66,
          "end": 206.9,
          "en": "to listen to changes in the navigator,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 206.9,
          "end": 209.96,
          "en": "React Navigation does give you ways of listening",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 209.96,
          "end": 213.66,
          "en": "to such changes, but I have a better solution here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 213.66,
          "end": 218.56,
          "en": "We keep on using context because that has the advantage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 218.56,
          "end": 223.56,
          "en": "that we can update the context once we fetched our expenses.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 223.8,
          "end": 226.43,
          "en": "And it means that we don't have to change all the code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 226.43,
          "end": 227.41,
          "en": "in all our app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 227.41,
          "end": 230.54,
          "en": "because we can keep on working with context.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 230.54,
          "end": 232.43,
          "en": "As an additional benefit,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 232.43,
          "end": 236.74,
          "en": "we have to send less HTTP requests because we, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 236.74,
          "end": 239.82,
          "en": "don't have to fetch new data from the backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 239.82,
          "end": 242.52,
          "en": "just because we added a new expense.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 242.52,
          "end": 244.71,
          "en": "Because when we add a new expense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 244.71,
          "end": 248.36,
          "en": "we already have all the data we entered here on the device,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 248.36,
          "end": 251.83,
          "en": "so fetching it again from the backend is a bit redundant.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 251.83,
          "end": 253.87,
          "en": "If we keep on using context",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 253.87,
          "end": 256.91,
          "en": "we utilize the data we already have on the device",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 256.91,
          "end": 259.25,
          "en": "and we just update everything offline",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 259.25,
          "end": 262.14,
          "en": "in addition to sending the data to the backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 262.14,
          "end": 264.89,
          "en": "But this saves us this extra request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 264.89,
          "end": 266.84,
          "en": "where we fetch the data again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 266.84,
          "end": 270.66,
          "en": "because we would only fetch the data again we already had.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 270.66,
          "end": 272.923,
          "en": "And that doesn't make a lot of sense.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 273.78,
          "end": 276.1,
          "en": "So for all these reasons,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 276.1,
          "end": 279.79,
          "en": "I wanna switch back to using context again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 279.79,
          "end": 282.24,
          "en": "And instead of managing my expenses here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 282.24,
          "end": 287.24,
          "en": "with state in recentExpenses, we can get rid of that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 287.53,
          "end": 291.47,
          "en": "and we simply add a new method to our context,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 291.47,
          "end": 295.46,
          "en": "a new method that allows us to set our expenses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 295.46,
          "end": 297.75,
          "en": "so that we don't just add a new expense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 297.75,
          "end": 301.78,
          "en": "but we also set expenses when we initially fetch them,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 301.78,
          "end": 304.33,
          "en": "so that when we at expenses from the backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 304.33,
          "end": 306.54,
          "en": "we can set them to our context",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 306.54,
          "end": 309.84,
          "en": "and then we work on these fetched and set expenses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 309.84,
          "end": 311.91,
          "en": "thereafter in the app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 311.91,
          "end": 313.53,
          "en": "So in expenses context,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 313.53,
          "end": 317.72,
          "en": "I will finally get rid of all that dummy data now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 317.72,
          "end": 320.27,
          "en": "because we don't need that anymore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 320.27,
          "end": 324.81,
          "en": "and I will add a new method here, setExpenses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 326.25,
          "end": 330.983,
          "en": "where I actually expect to get my expenses as an array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 333.61,
          "end": 337.17,
          "en": "And I will add a new reducer case here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 337.17,
          "end": 339.9,
          "en": "SET could be a fitting name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 339.9,
          "end": 343.94,
          "en": "where I return my new state and my new state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 343.94,
          "end": 346.33,
          "en": "that I want to return here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 346.33,
          "end": 350.11,
          "en": "should simply be my action payload",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 350.11,
          "end": 352.25,
          "en": "because I expect my action payload",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 352.25,
          "end": 355.883,
          "en": "to be that array of expenses, which I wanna use here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 357.23,
          "end": 361.47,
          "en": "And then here in the expenses context provider",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 361.47,
          "end": 364.083,
          "en": "we can add a new function, setExpenses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 366.963,
          "end": 369.16,
          "en": "and we get our expenses here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 369.16,
          "end": 372.85,
          "en": "and we then dispatch a new object of type SET",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 372.85,
          "end": 375.223,
          "en": "which is the type I used in the re-user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 376.73,
          "end": 380.33,
          "en": "And our payload is equal to those expenses here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 380.33,
          "end": 381.89300000000003,
          "en": "which we get as a parameter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 383.04,
          "end": 388.04,
          "en": "Now we add dysfunction to our object here, our value object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 388.37,
          "end": 390.04,
          "en": "So we add setExpenses here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 390.04,
          "end": 393.453,
          "en": "and point at the newly added setExpenses function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 394.3,
          "end": 398.01,
          "en": "And then thereafter as a final step in recentEexpenses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 399.09000000000003,
          "end": 403.15,
          "en": "we want to use our expenses context",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 404.07,
          "end": 408.14,
          "en": "and execute setExpenses here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 408.14,
          "end": 412.763,
          "en": "and forward our expenses which we fetched like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 413.6,
          "end": 418.6,
          "en": "With that done, if we save everything, I get an error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 419.73,
          "end": 423.19,
          "en": "Yeah, of course, we still have the dummy expenses here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 423.19,
          "end": 426.25,
          "en": "in the context, we need to get rid of those.",
          "zh": ""
